{"title": "Ask HN: Syncthing", "link": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50528871", "summary": "<p>Syncthing on Android. Since the original developers pulled out of Android I've been using a fork named Syncthing-fork maintained by who knows, on F-Droid.<p>Now I just learned that has been pulled from F-Droid. What are people on HN doing to run Syncthing on Android? Honestly Syncthing has been one of the lowest effort apps that I used. I've set it up on all my devices and the thing keeps working through device churn, sort of an \"distributed setup of Theseus\".<p>So what do people do now?</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50528871\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50528871</a></p>\n<p>Points: 1</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>", "published": "2026-11-17T08:27:36+00:00", "source": "Hacker News Best", "category": "techblog", "matched_entities": {}, "ontology": {"repo": "BlogRadar", "category": "techblog", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "source_event_model": "blog_post", "event_model_id": "tech.blog_post", "evidence_policy_ids": ["source_metadata", "article_text"], "event_model_payload": {"headline": "Ask HN: Syncthing", "source_name": "Hacker News Best", "source_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50528871", "published_at": "2026-11-17T08:27:36+00:00", "summary": "<p>Syncthing on Android. Since the original developers pulled out of Android I've been using a fork named Syncthing-fork maintained by who knows, on F-Droid.<p>Now I just learned that has been pulled from F-Droid. What are people on HN doing to run Syncthing on Android? Honestly Syncthing has been one of the lowest effort apps that I used. I've set it up on all my devices and the thing keeps working through device churn, sort of an \"distributed setup of Theseus\".<p>So what do people do now?</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50528871\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50528871</a></p>\n<p>Points: 1</p>\n<p># Comm